A||||21||Richard Parnell||Smoked Not a Viper but a Ninja type bike||||6||
Z||000000||Richard Parnell||11-28-2000||04:09 PM||||Haven't yet had a good run with anyone on the road yet.  But this morning was coming up a long hill towards work, I had two cars in front of me no one coming from the other direction so I pulled out to pass.  I had several cars behind me and as I pulled out I could see one of those Ninja type bikes with the guy all hunched over almast laying down on the thing swing out a couple of cars back.  As I passed the two cars in front of me, I could see him coming, so I eased it into 4th and put the throttle about 3/4 down.  The 350 has a ripping sound when the 4 barrels open up.  It was sweet.  I looked back and the bike was about 1/4 mile back.  We were moving pretty good.  Don't know how fast though cause I still haven't figured out what's wrong with my speedo since the conversion.||||reg||6
Z||000001||JohnnyK||11-28-2000||06:23 PM||||I'm sorry to be the one to tell you this but a sport bike would eat you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||11-28-2000||07:32 PM||||A ninja 250 isnt really that fast for top end.  A Fiero with a 350 should be able to keep up I would think.<P>I am not certain but I think my GPz 550 wasnt as fast as my first motor and the 4:10 tranny(pretty sure my current motor/tranny would get hosed hardcore).  I know the Fiero has a higher top speed than my 550.||||reg||1
