Z||000005||rockcrawl||11-28-2000||08:48 PM||||I had a ZX6 Ninja (600cc), piped and jetted, and I have never been in any car that could even come close to the acceleration that thing had. I didn't have the guts to top it out, but I hit 130 and there was plenty more. I also owned the 350 TPI Countach (2910lbs) at the same time and it never would have kept up with the bike. So I'd say you did pretty good to whoop the bike like that. I wonder what it was.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Also, I feel a lot safer at 100MPH+ when I'm on four wheels and enclosed. I hit a deer at about 40 MPH with that same bike, and it wasn't fun. I don't think I ever felt totally safe on a bike again. <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000006||count_iblis||11-28-2000||10:27 PM||||sorry to say this also but a sport bike would eat you <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Greg Piet||11-29-2000||01:45 AM||||I again must get involved, a sport bike is too general...<P>You are trying to tell me that a ninja 250 (which technically is a sport bike) can hose a Fiero with a chevy 350 in it(straight line as most highways can be considered to be in general)?<P>IF SO...<BR>I am curious the following<BR>1/4 mile times of the two<BR>and top speed of the two<BR>AND <BR>time to reach 90% of top speed (or thereabouts)<P>I wouldnt even dare to mention that a CBR600 will lose to a fairly stock naturally aspirated 4bbl 350 in a Fiero(those CBR's are badass in my book).  But I DO KNOW of a Fiero that has a naturally aspirated Vette motor (with lots of goodies) that can hose most sport bikes (accel and top speed), with a possible exception to an 1100 cc sportbike.  This was proven when there was a sportbike race next to our autocross at the local speedway...  the CBR900 got hosed and the ninja 1100 tried but couldnt quite cut the mustard.  None of these cars were set up for dragracing, but that was the competition agreed upon, and it ended when they felt they ran out of road.  The bikes were winning the first FEW seconds though but it was tight.  There is also a twin turbo RX-7 that could have given the bikes a run for their money as well, but he did not want to encourage the little bikers.<P>Last I checked a Ninja 1100 topped out at about 180mph, well this Fiero im mentioning has gone in excess of 210mph (controlled environment I must add).<BR>  <BR>My 2.8 doesnt have a snowballs chance against  a new sportbike (i dont even think a 250), but when I pass a tractor trailer at 110 (like thats gonna happen) I will still be on the road.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||afRaceR||11-29-2000||02:02 AM||||I used to own a ninja 250 with a stage 3 K&N jet kit and a full race Yoshimura exhaust. I beat so many people, word got around, and hardly anybody would ever race me. It got so bad, only other sport bikes would race and I know it couldn't handle a CBR 600.||||reg||1
Z||000009||olympic||11-29-2000||03:34 AM||||  The guys over at ls1.com say they beat ~600cc bikes all the time on the freeway.  Most of it is probably due to lack of experience on the bikers part.  From a dead stop though the bike has a huge advantage. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fieroboy1||11-29-2000||08:33 PM||||First off who rides a girly bike like a ninja 250????  Most of the bikes out there are zx6's and 7's pretty much 600/750 bikes.  NO WAY are you going to beat something with 110-120hp and weighs 400 lbs.  My buddys R1 has 190 hp and weighs 380 lbs or so. Unless the guy was asleep at the handlebars or you passed a moped  You aren't going to touch a decent streetbike. (250's EXCLUDED)||||reg||1
