Z||000012||gixxer||11-29-2000||10:02 PM||||Ah yes, found it.<BR>Here are the Cycle magazine road test results for a 1988 Suzuki GSX-R 750 "Slingshot", which I have an example of, and is in fine (uncrashed still) health.<BR>Rear wheel HP: 91<BR>Claimed crank horsepower: 108 (from a Brit magazine)<BR>Redline 13,000 RPM, Tach starts at 3,000 =)<BR>0-60: 2.85 seconds<BR>1/4 mile: 11.04 @ 122.41 MPH<BR>Measured top speed:152 MPH<BR>The sub powerband starts at 6,000, the real powerband begins at 9,000 and goes to 12,500.<BR>While not cutting edge performance anymore, it serves me well. Some modifications from Yoshimura have enhanced its capabilities a bit.<BR>I certainly wouldn't hesitate to race any car if the road conditions were right.<BR>OK, done bragging. ||||reg||1
