Z||000016||Slammed Fiero||11-30-2000||12:19 AM||||210mph in a Fiero...... What tranny does it use??? This is highly doubtful ...a McLaren F1 has 600+hp V12 and it tops out at 230mph , it's designed to go that fast.<P>This just sounds like a big fish story.... 210mph...ZR1 405hp , 188mph <BR>Viper 450hp 191mph <BR>After 200mph it took John Lingenfelter an extra 50hp to go another 8mph according to an article ihave on his yellow Zr1......<P><BR>Jonathan McCreery||||reg||1
Z||000017||jlhuber||11-30-2000||12:49 AM||||I have to agree with Fieroboy1 and all others who say a 350'd fiero could NOT beat a bike.  HA!... and I'm Santa Clause.  Same arguement as the Fiero story... have you ever driven/ridden one?  If not, quit talkin the smack that you don't know.  If you have, and you still say the Fiero would win, that must be one helluva Fiero. ..can I watch?  If you have never ridden a "crotch-rocket" as we call 'em [any of the following series: Kawasaki ZX, Honda CBR, Yamaha R, SUZKI GSX(R)], how do you know how fast they really are.  Now when you start pitting a heavily modified Fiero or Vette or similar against a bone stock crotch-rocket, there is a good chance that the car could win.  Out of curiosity, how do you know that he was trying co catch/race you?  Maybe he was just passing everyone like you were.  How hard was he on the throttle?  It is kind of like me taking a Syclone against a Rice-boy at a stoplight.  Yeah, I blew by him off the line, but did the Rice-boy even really want to race in the first place? (granted that most do, but still)  I don't doubt that a Fiero with a 350 will scoot, it is just that ...a bike!?!  This is one that I'll have to see to believe.  Anyway, that is my $0.02 worth.  Say what you will, my opinion is my opinion and it remains till my eyes view the merchandise.  Sheeit, "Beer Run!".  Later peps||||reg||13
Z||000018||Joe4x4||11-30-2000||07:21 AM||||Hey ,.....wanna race tittle for tittle<BR>I do have a CBR-900-RR ...I had this bike out to 170 .....high 10`s at Atco raceway N.J.<P>I`ll race you and than I`ll have another Fiero to my collection .... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>only funnin||||reg||6
Z||000019||ChadMan||11-30-2000||09:41 AM||||Yeah, I'd have to guess there's only two kinds of sportbikes a V8 Fiero could smoke:<P>1) Small-displacement sportbikes (Ninja 250, Suz GS500e, etc)<BR>2) Larger-displacement sportbikes ridden by newbies who don't know their bikes make no power below 6000 rpm, and therefore don't downshift when it's time to race<P>Gotta disagree with the idea that a Ninja 250 is a "girly bike" though.  They may not be balls-out fast like the 600-and-up bikes, but they handle great and they're lots of fun, like a moped on steroids.  A lot of girls do ride them, but so do a lot of guys getting started out in amateur roadracing.<P>I've actually considered trading my Maxim 750 for a Ninja 250.  It's a lot cheaper to go racing on two wheels than on four.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Richard Parnell||12-01-2000||07:58 PM||||Well, that certainly got a rise out of a number of people.  I really don't know what kind of Ninja bike the guy had.  Tho it's of the type I've seen before and know they're pretty fast and he was coming to pass me.  Now I'm not saying my car is the fastest thing around but it'll do for me.  It actaully scares me a bit.  I rarely stomp it.  It just seems to be more fun to cruise with the nice sound from the pipes. I haven't posted pics yet but i will.  The HP I'm not sure of but it's over 200 but well under 300.  The mechanic who did most of the work (Bob Sato) has a silver GT that has 410 HP in it, it is undriveable in my opinion but he does it. For you guys that will question the HP rating i have to say right now I don't know if that's 410 HP at the wheels , clutch (or where ever) or the tip of his nose.  Though he has raced and beaten those 1100cc bikes. It idles like some dragster and I don't care for that as a daily driver.  I think even now my car is a little bit on the loud sid and I may put some flowmasters on it. It only has glasspacks on it now. Anyway it was interesting seeing everyone's opinions.||||reg||6
Z||000021||Sillhouette.com||12-01-2000||11:40 PM||||Sorry to burst your bubble but I don't believe a fiero is able of 210mph and still stay on terra firma.  My last wind tunnel tests have put the critical speed at 173mph after that you best have pilot licences and some wings or you'll be mentioned at the Darwin awards.  <BR>On the next note a viper engine that puts out 450 hp roughly.  I'm sure there are much more feasble ways to get that much horse power for a Fiero.  The downfall of the fiero is weight so you tell me that V10 engine fiero can outaccelerate a sport bike not likely.  I have seen a 911 turbo beaten by a sports bike the one that you basically lay on<P>Later||||reg||1
